1
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,797
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:29,880
YAMU!

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

4
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:04,799
Don't worry, Yugi.

5
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:05,957
He couldn't have gotten far.

6
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,237
We've got to find him.

7
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:10,477
Pegasus is the only one who
can restore Grandpa's soul.

8
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:11,390
Wait a minute.

9
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:13,850
Why?

10
00:01:13,933 --> 00:01:14,763
What's the matter, Taya?

11
00:01:14,846 --> 00:01:15,797
Well, that tower.

12
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:16,777
It looks...

13
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:17,720
Yeah, go on.

14
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:21,295
I think I've been there before
with Tristan and Bacora.

15
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:23,500
I vaguely recall a secret room.

16
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:24,978
Pegasus' sanctuary.

17
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,817
Maybe it was just a dream, but...

18
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,277
Only if we were both dreaming.

19
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,537
I'm starting to remember it, too.

20
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:33,237
Pegasus fought with Bakura, and
then Bakura's evil spirit came out.

21
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:34,517
But why did we forget?

22
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,440
Evil spirit?

23
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:38,719
Yeah, I bet he cast a spell on you.

24
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,017
Well, we remember now.

25
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:40,930
Let's go.

26
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:43,940
Hey! Wait up!

27
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,120
It's all over.

28
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:52,311
Everything I've struggled to
obtain is now beyond my grasp.

29
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:55,291
Keeping their souls will not serve me now.

30
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,317
Besides, I'm a man of my word.

31
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,617
And because of the defeat
I suffered at the hands of

32
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,697
Yugi and the mysterious spirit
of his Millennium Puzzle,

33
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:06,560
I am duty-bound to fulfill my pledge.

34
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:11,660
And so, I release these three souls.

35
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,420
Cecilia, I'm sorry, but I have failed you.

36
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,577
My attempt to take over Kyber Corp,

37
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:24,777
my efforts to get all the Millennium
Items was all done for you.

38
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:27,978
in the hopes that I could
restore you, body and soul.

39
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,040
How sweet.

40
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,160
Huh? Who's there?

41
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:34,490
Akurov.

42
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:35,960
I remember now.

43
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:39,755
You, you're the one that
possesses the Millennium Ring.

44
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,620
Yes, and I intend to have all the items.

45
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:44,697
Care to wager yours on a shadow game?

46
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:47,780
I'll give you a second
chance at a Millennium item.

47
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:52,428
What you couldn't win from Yugi,
perhaps you can win from me.

48
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:53,857
Who knows?

49
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,100
If you defeat me and claim my ring,

50
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:59,927
your deepest desires might not
be beyond your grasp after all.

51
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:08,477
Your Millennium Item allows you to
look into people's minds, Pegasus.

52
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,854
Mine allows me to see into their souls.

53
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,597
I have but to look at your deck, Pegasus,
and it reveals to me your true nature.

54
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,320
The Happy Lover card.

55
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:20,860
It shows you have
experienced the joys of love.

56
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:25,920
However, this card is upside down, which
means your romance ended in tragedy.

57
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,320
What a pity it is.

58
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:32,853
Well, the next card should show me
more about your present than your past.

59
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:35,400
Ah, the Mask of Darkness, eh?

60
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:40,771
So your recent actions were all just
an effort to mask your true objectives.

61
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,457
Objectives that came from
deep within your heart.

62
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:48,600
Who would have thought you even had a heart,
let alone one so easily broken? Quiet.

63
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:50,411
Let's just play the game.

64
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,160
As you wish.

65
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:56,320
But first, there is one
more card to be revealed.

66
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Don't you want to see your future?

67
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,260
Doma, the Angel of Silence.

68
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:06,840
It's an appropriate card for your future,
since I will now silence you forever.

69
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:12,402
Prepare yourself, mortal, for a shadow game
the likes of which you've never played.

70
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:16,934
This match will be played on
the landscape of our minds.

71
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:23,237
really now pegasus is
that all you can muster ah

72
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,617
but you've been fatigued
by your shadow duel with

73
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:30,417
yugi your mind is weary
while mine is fresh you are

74
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,217
defeated a rank amateur
to one whom has played for

75
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:36,717
centuries you've lived
for centuries what kind of

76
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:40,477
creature are you i am the
one who will possess all the

77
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,757
millennium items and i shall
use their combined might

78
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:47,260
to conquer the entire world
You have lost the game,

79
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:52,680
and that entitles me to take your Millennium
Item the way you meant to take Yugi's.

80
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,860
No! No!

81
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,071
Did you hear that scream?

82
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,713
It came from the tower!

83
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,272
It sounded like Pegasus!

84
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,010
Look!

85
00:05:12,093 --> 00:05:12,975
Something's happened!

86
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:14,770
It's him!

87
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,380
Croquet, what happened to Pegasus?

88
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,657
It's none of your concern.

89
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:22,152
He's suddenly taken ill.

90
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,277
But what about Grandpa and the others?

91
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,937
He promised he'd free their souls.

92
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:26,850
He promised!

93
00:05:26,933 --> 00:05:27,763
Not my department.

94
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,779
Hey, did you get a look at Pegasus?

95
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:34,177
Who or what could have done that to him?

96
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,090
I don't know.

97
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:36,817
Maybe we should check out
the towers, you think?

98
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,697
So this is where Pegasus hangs out?

99
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,837
Whoever that woman is, she sure is pretty.

100
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,750
Yeah.

101
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,920
Hey, what's this?

102
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,360
It seems to be a diary.

103
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:50,099
Maybe we'll find something in here.

104
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,917
It's all about Pegasus. Listen to this.

105
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,397
He's written about that lady.

106
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,500
She's everywhere.

107
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:59,075
She seems to be very important to him.

108
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:04,377
Darling Cecilia, at last I've finally
found a way to restore you to this world.

109
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:07,578
It's an elaborate plan, but
not one beyond my genius.

110
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,497
It involves the Kaiba Corporation
and some ancient magic

111
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:13,297
I plan to harness when I
obtain more Millennium items.

112
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,680
This could be it.

113
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:18,417
This might explain why he set up the
tournament and why he went after Yugi.

114
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,088
And maybe who this girl is.

115
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:22,573
It's pretty obvious he's hung up on her.

116
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,510
Cecilia.

117
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,137
Oh, my lovely darling.

118
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,157
Darling, Cecilia.

119
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:31,960
You know how I've loved you since the
first moment we met those many years ago.

120
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:34,040
I'll never forget that day.

121
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:37,180
It was at a party at my
father's country estate.

122
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:42,640
It was a gala event with celebrities
and tycoons from all over the world.

123
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:45,360
Anyone who was anyone was there.

124
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:49,880
But by far, the one that
impressed me most was you.

125
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:54,000
Even though we were only
children, I knew I was in love.

126
00:06:54,540 --> 00:07:00,160
We were drawn to each other, and from
that moment on, we were inseparable,

127
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,250
you and I.

128
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:04,440
You inflamed my passions,

129
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:08,662
inspired me to become a painter,
and you were my favorite subject.

130
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:13,940
I was so in love, and just when I
thought things couldn't get any better,

131
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:19,060
you agreed to take my hand once
again, this time in marriage.

132
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:24,220
That was the happiest day of
my life, but it was cut short,

133
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:26,714
for it seemed just as we said our vows,

134
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:31,800
you were struck down by a devastating
disease, and taken from me and this world.

135
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:35,100
It was as if a blow had
struck me from the heavens.

136
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,517
I was filled with sorrow.

137
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,320
From that moment on, I
could no longer paint.

138
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:42,800
My heart grew bitter and cold.

139
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:47,157
Unable to accept the idea that our
life together was forever lost,

140
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:50,117
I decided to scour the
earth in an attempt to

141
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:53,360
find any way to reach you
beyond this mortal veil.

142
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:57,645
My journey eventually brought me
to the great pyramids of Egypt,

143
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:00,357
that mysterious land
whose These ancient people

144
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,969
believed in a life
beyond the here and now,

145
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,020
a belief I wanted to embrace.

146
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:10,220
I had just begun to explore that
ancient city when fate intervened.

147
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:16,660
Thank you.

148
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:18,760
Stranger, heed my advice.

149
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:24,020
You have journeyed far, seeking
to cure the ache within your soul.

150
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,740
Take great care.

151
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:32,481
The search to heal the pains of a broken
heart might lead to only greater heartache.

152
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:36,880
Wait, how do you know? It matters
not. Go home. But I couldn't.

153
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:41,354
I realized if he somehow knew of my
pain, maybe he could help me heal it.

154
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:43,457
I followed him against his wishes.

155
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:44,820
Or so I thought.

156
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:52,957
Although the passage seemed to lead to
the bowels of the earth, still I followed.

157
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,677
And my footsteps led me to a hidden crypt.

158
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:59,054
but apparently buried beneath
centuries of civilization.

159
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,160
What is this place?

160
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:04,576
So, you chose not to heed my warning.

161
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,500
What are you doing? Let me go!

162
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:12,840
I am a guardian of the Millennium Items.

163
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:17,877
Once this sacred place has been discovered,
the only way to leave is to be chosen.

164
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,440
It must be your destiny.

165
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,737
But how could these Millennium
Items be part of my destiny?

166
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:23,820
What do you mean?

167
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:28,600
You will now be tested by the
item itself, the Millennium Eye.

168
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:32,560
The Eye itself?

169
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:33,620
But how?

170
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:39,280
Each Millennium Item awaits the day its
fated possessor appears to claim it,

171
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:42,080
and punishes those who are undeserving.

172
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,550
Punishes?

173
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:44,930
Now,

174
00:09:45,013 --> 00:09:49,577
if you pass its test, it will empower you
to see more than you've ever seen before.

175
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,177
And if I fail its test?

176
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,597
If you are not the one
destined to possess it,

177
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:57,092
all that awaits you is nightmares
beyond your imagination.

178
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:11,500
You have not descended
into chaos and madness.

179
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,417
You are the chosen one.

180
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:17,600
Now your eyes will be opened to
dimensions beyond the here and now,

181
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:22,428
like having a sixth sense, capable of
seeing worlds and times outside our own.

182
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:25,110
Cecilia!

183
00:10:25,193 --> 00:10:27,000
Maximilian, it's really you!

184
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,700
Cecilia, I found you.

185
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:38,820
My darling, we're reunited at long last.

186
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:43,060
But be warned, seeing's not the
same as touching, holding, being...

187
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:46,482
That is beyond the power
of this Millennium Item.

188
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:49,781
I should have once again
been engulfed by despair.

189
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:55,400
But seeing you for that brief moment gave
me more hope than I thought possible.

190
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,617
Even though you were gone from my world,

191
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,837
I knew there was still a
way to reach your spirit.

192
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,397
And I wouldn't rest till I
found a way to bring you back.

193
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,362
And once again,

194
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:07,619
touch the flower that is your face
and gaze into your eyes once more.

195
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:11,577
It goes on to say that later,
Pegasus got an inspiration.

196
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:15,417
He found a way to combine
Kaiba's virtual technology

197
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,740
with the magic of Millennium
items to restore Cecilia.

198
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:23,140
But nothing about Grandpa or
the Kaiba brothers. Hey, look!

199
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,813
Three soul cards, and they're all blank!

200
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:27,877
Pegasus must have freed them!

201
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,280
Let's find out! Yeah!

202
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,840
I hope they're okay.
Come on, Yuv. Let's go!

203
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:37,380
Hold on! Wait for me!

204
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:40,170
Huh?

205
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:44,000
Wh-what's going on?

206
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,940
He has a Millennium Item, too!

207
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:53,595
The disturbance in the mystic
alignment brings me here.

208
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,040
Who are you? Huh?

209
00:11:56,860 --> 00:12:01,540
I know not who has stolen Pegasus'
Millennium Eye and upset the cosmic balance,

210
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:03,977
but perhaps I should begin my search here.

211
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,137
Through the centuries,

212
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:07,217
those who have come to
possess one Millennium

213
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:09,917
Item have often been
driven to covet them all.

214
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,977
No! Stay back!

215
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:14,766
I sense that the thief hides
somewhere within the castle walls.

216
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:17,627
I shall begin my
investigation with this boy.

217
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,998
What are you doing?

218
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:23,961
The Millennium Key will unlock his
mind and reveal the truth to me.

219
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,110
Huh?

220
00:12:35,193 --> 00:12:36,023
What is this?

221
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,860
This youth's mind contains two chambers.

222
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,977
Never have I seen such a thing.

223
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:44,320
One is a room of a pure
innocence, devoid of malice.

224
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:47,457
The purity of soul I sense
here could not possibly

225
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:50,658
belong to the criminal that
stole the Millennium Eye.

226
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,497
But wait.

227
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:55,920
In the other chamber, I
detect another presence,

228
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,920
and this soul is much more mysterious.

229
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,120
It's all right.

230
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:04,479
You may enter my chamber
if that is what you desire.

231
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:07,001
But I warn you, tread cautiously.

232
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:10,828
I will allow no harm to come to
the boy whose vessel I share.

233
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:13,500
Your presence here intrigues me.

234
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:18,113
In the past, I've ventured
into the minds of many people,

235
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:21,749
but I've never encountered a
chamber so dank and mysterious.

236
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:25,547
I feel as though I'm in a tomb
of an ancient Egyptian pharaoh.

237
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,817
I don't know how you entered my mind.

238
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:30,257
Explain yourself before
you trespass further.

239
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,869
I demand an explanation
for your intrusion.

240
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,765
I seek a criminal who has stolen
the power of a Millennium Item.

241
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:40,977
It has been five long millennia since
those ancient items were created.

242
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:44,737
Their magical energies were
trapped in them by a brave pharaoh.

243
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:49,417
Combined, these seven Millennium Items
possess power enough to conquer the world.

244
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:53,735
Hence, many evil men have ventured
to gather these items for themselves.

245
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:57,740
It is my heritage to guard
the Millennium Items,

246
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:02,280
and my charge to punish the thief
who stole Pegasus' Millennium Eye.

247
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:05,080
And you accuse me of being that criminal?

248
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,317
You have already taken refuge
in the vessel of another.

249
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:09,812
That does not bode well.

250
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:14,237
But if you are not the criminal, then
you have nothing to fear from my search.

251
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:18,600
Guilty until proven innocent, an
ancient concept for this modern age.

252
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:21,320
However, I have nothing to hide.

253
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,894
I'm not your criminal.

254
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:27,000
Then grant me passage to
your unconscious mind. Fine.

255
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:28,927
I'll open the doors for you.

256
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:32,428
You may search them to
your heart's content.

257
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:36,470
Hmm.

258
00:14:36,553 --> 00:14:39,740
Never have I seen such
complexity as in this one's mind.

259
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:42,592
Truly, he is an extraordinary individual.

260
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:45,640
And now, I will leave
you to your exploration.

261
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:50,060
There are mysteries within mysteries here.

262
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:51,740
Levels beyond levels.

263
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:54,560
So I must probe each
chamber for the truth.

264
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:04,537
it was a trap despite his cooperation
something in his mind conspires

265
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:08,797
to keep me from the truth so
many doors so many false entries

266
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:13,097
all designed to distract me from
the proper path but no matter how

267
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:17,121
they try to confuse and disorient
me my millennium key will show me

268
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,830
the true way.

269
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,480
It draws me here.

270
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,877
The truth lies within.

271
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,657
It appears safe enough.

272
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:26,570
Still,

273
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:36,097
I shall proceed with extreme caution.

274
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:37,137
Another trap.

275
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:39,760
Never have I seen mental defenses so

276
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,230
strong.

277
00:15:41,313 --> 00:15:42,580
This could be the end of me.

278
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:53,860
If I fall into this deep darkness,

279
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:56,977
I will be trapped eternally
within this cryptic mind.

280
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:59,697
I don't know why the spirit of
my puzzle's doing this to you,

281
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,486
but I can't let him hurt you.

282
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:02,770
Huh?

283
00:16:02,853 --> 00:16:03,683
It's the innocent one.

284
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:05,060
Let me help you up.

285
00:16:06,620 --> 00:16:09,620
I seek only the truth, but it's strange.

286
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:10,839
My way is blocked.

287
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:12,357
It's strange, all right,

288
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:16,077
but I don't think the spirit of the
puzzle is doing this on purpose.

289
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:19,497
I get the feeling that there are
some memories hidden even from him.

290
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:21,580
I sure wish I knew what they were.

291
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:23,970
Huh?

292
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:30,560
The door, it opens for you, as if seeking
to answer your curiosity. But why?

293
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:32,340
Why does it yield to you?

294
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,520
What is all this?

295
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:37,800
What are these stone tablets?

296
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:42,737
5,000 years ago, Egyptian kings played
a game of great and terrible power.

297
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:47,020
These shadow games were played
with real magic and real monsters.

298
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:51,937
But those games erupted into a war that
threatened to destroy the entire world.

299
00:16:52,020 --> 00:16:57,220
Until a brave pharaoh locked the magic
away, sealing the monsters in stone tablets.

300
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:01,597
But how could your other personality
have knowledge of this ancient history?

301
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:05,100
And why do I suddenly sense
here, in his unconscious mind,

302
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:08,516
magic that the world has not
known for five millennia?

303
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:13,175
They look just like the monsters on
the cards we use to play with today.

304
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,220
Look out!

305
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,360
A new threat appears.

306
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,160
The Dark Magician!

307
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,580
He prepares to strike.

308
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,980
He's another mental defense
against any intruders.

309
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:31,180
The Magician intends to
destroy us both. No way!

310
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:35,133
Unless we can stop him, we
will never leave this chamber.

311
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:36,490
Wait.

312
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:39,997
This surface on which I stand may
be the means of our salvation.

313
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:40,910
him.

314
00:17:40,993 --> 00:17:43,157
If that other image spawned the
essence of the Dark Magician,

315
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:46,317
then this one must contain the
magical energy of his nemesis,

316
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,917
the Blue Eyes White Dragon.

317
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,471
If I can use the power of

318
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:54,617
the Millennium Key to unleash its
might, it will obliterate the Magician.

319
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:55,560
No, stop!

320
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:56,810
Why

321
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,450
should I?

322
00:17:59,533 --> 00:18:01,357
Because he'd never hurt me.

323
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:04,100
Dark Magician, we are not intruders.

324
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,517
Don't you You recognize me?

325
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,817
Stand aside and let us leave in peace.

326
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:11,180
We will not reveal the
hidden secrets. You know me.

327
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:12,720
You trust me.

328
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:14,720
What's this?

329
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,617
The dark magician,

330
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:21,876
who in ancient times obeyed only the
pharaoh, gives heed to this youth?

331
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:25,620
Impossible, unless this
boy is the chosen one.

332
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:28,080
The prophecy comes to pass.

333
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:40,900
I apologize for my rude
intrusion into your mind.

334
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:43,997
I did not realize that you are
the Chosen One and that the

335
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:47,374
ancient predictions have
finally been fulfilled at last.

336
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:50,997
In my search for a thief, I
instead found the most worthy,

337
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,080
one fated to unlock all the magic.

338
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,797
The theft of Pegasus'
Millennium Eye was but the

339
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:58,437
first sign that evil once
again walks the Earth,

340
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,657
bringing madness in its wake.

341
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:05,000
As in ancient times, Chaos once more
threatens to envelop an unsuspecting world.

342
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:08,573
And only he who solved the
Millennium Puzzle can save it.

343
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,120
What do you mean?

344
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:13,161
Is there anything else you
can tell me about this?

345
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:15,180
Take great care.

346
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,540
Be on your guard.

347
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:19,837
For whoever the thief is who
stole Pegasus' Millennium Item,

348
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:21,802
he will also come seeking yours.

349
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:24,477
Wow, that's almost too
scary to think about.

350
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:28,337
But if a guy like you couldn't
find him, how do you expect me to?

351
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:29,440
Wait, don't go.

352
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,365
I've got a lot more questions.

353
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:33,700
Like, who are you?

354
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:38,056
My name is Shadi, and I am certain
that we will meet again another day.

355
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,100
But until then, stay true to your destiny.

356
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:44,874
Remember, the fate of the
world rests on your shoulders.
